WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.960
The latest trailer for Infinity War has arrived​,
and it's packed with even more action than

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:05.960
before.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:10.410
With a ton of all-new, epic moments thundering
across the screen, some less obvious details

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.620
are bound to slip through the cracks.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:16.810
Here are the small details you may have missed
in the new Infinity War trailer.

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:18.240
Half the universe

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:23.220
While the first trailer had Thanos waxing
poetic about his dream of "balancing the universe,"

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:27.449
it was still pretty vague about just how he
intended to do that.

00:00:27.449 --> 00:00:31.330
Now, Gamora spells out for us exactly what
he plans to do:

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:35.500
"He only ever had one goal: to wipe out half the
universe.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:41.399
If he gets all the Infinity Stones, he can
do it with the snap of his fingers."

00:00:41.399 --> 00:00:45.990
Longtime comics​ readers know what's up:
When Thanos assembled the full power of the

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:51.629
stones in the 1991 comic event Infinity Gauntlet,
his first order of business was to make half

00:00:51.629 --> 00:00:55.310
of all life in the universe suddenly vanish
without warning.

00:00:55.310 --> 00:01:00.379
He did this in order to impress Marvel’s
Death, who in the comics is a sexy undead

00:01:00.379 --> 00:01:04.210
being he would very much like to smooch.

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:08.180
It seems our heroes will have a bit more of
an advance warning in the movie, but will

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:12.009
they be able to stop Thanos before his fateful
finger snap?

00:01:12.009 --> 00:01:13.970
Loki’s betrayal

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:19.100
In the last few minutes of Thor: Ragnarok,
Loki deftly lifted the Tesseract from Odin’s

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.210
treasure room.

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:24.990
As the Asgardians journeyed into space away
from the ruins of their home, Loki and Thor

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:27.869
seemed to at last truly make amends.

00:01:27.869 --> 00:01:29.700
Or did they?

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:33.921
The new Infinity War trailer finds the God
of Mischief seemingly ready to surrender the

00:01:33.921 --> 00:01:35.579
Tesseract willingly.

00:01:35.579 --> 00:01:40.320
The so-called "Space Stone" is likely what
will allow the Mad Titan to warp to Earth.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:41.610
What’s Loki’s endgame?

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:46.760
It’s impossible to guess, considering he
has a penchant for double-, triple-, and quadruple-crosses.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:52.060
"Surprise!"

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:54.439
New Order

00:01:54.439 --> 00:01:59.259
The Black Order is Thanos’ elite squad of
lieutenants, charged with doing the kind of

00:01:59.259 --> 00:02:03.700
nitty gritty dirty work he wouldn’t touch
with a ten-foot Infinity Gauntlet.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:09.060
Their onscreen incarnation includes strategist
Corvus Glaive, the vicious Proxima Midnight,

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:13.400
the massive Cull Obsidian, and the slippery
Ebony Maw.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:17.980
While we can only glimpse the assembled group
briefly in the trailer, Ebony Maw gets special

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:18.980
attention.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:23.890
He may be in the midst of manipulating the
power of Doctor Strange to facilitate Thanos’

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:27.840
invasion, which is something he's done before
in the comics.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:29.040
Tiny Gamora?

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:33.990
The two Guardians of the Galaxy movies have
built an epic backstory of family drama behind

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:36.490
Thanos and his daughters, Gamora and Nebula.

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:40.290
It’s a bitter tale of abuse, betrayal, and
attempted murder.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:44.810
The new Infinity War trailer provides a surprising
moment of family bonding.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:49.660
We see Thanos take a tiny green hand in his
giant purple one, as he walks with a young

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:52.280
girl toward an ornate archway.

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:57.140
It seems like a safe bet that the girl is
a young Gamora, but is this a flashback?

00:02:57.140 --> 00:03:00.180
Maybe some weirdness via the Infinity Stones?

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.650
Thanos gets his helmet

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:06.160
Since his first appearance during the end
credits of The Avengers, Thanos’ look has

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:09.160
been tweaked, but he remains instantly recognizable.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:14.080
But when the first Infinity War trailer hit,
many comic book fans were plagued with one

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:16.430
question: where’s his helmet?

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:19.700
Something about that big, bald head just felt
wrong.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:25.340
Fortunately, the new trailer shows off multiple
shots that find his shiny hat firmly in place,

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:26.900
or freshly removed.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.010
Where’s Hawkeye?

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:34.760
Marvel is touting Infinity War as “the culmination​
of the entire Marvel Cinematic Universe​​,”

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:38.760
providing a grand clash of as many heroes
and villains as can fit into two-and-a-half

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.980
hours of IMAX-sized action.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.680
"I know all your names."

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:49.780
The new trailer includes just about all of
our leading stars, but one of the original

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:52.500
Avengers is still conspicuously missing.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:57.020
Jeremy Renner is confirmed to be back once
more as Clint Barton, a.k.a. Hawkeye, but

00:03:57.020 --> 00:04:02.050
none of Infinity War’s marketing has shown
even a single one of Hawkeye's mighty purple

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:03.050
feathers.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:06.630
It would be strange if this founding member
of the cinematic Avengers didn’t have a

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:08.980
major role to play in this big payoff.

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:14.170
Directors Joe and Anthony Russo remain tight-lipped
on the subject of Clint, hinting only that

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:16.880
he has a “special spot” in the film.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:21.560
Let's hope he actually stays alive and doesn't
get… well… shafted.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:22.700
Thanks for watching!

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:25.180
